From 1c33c69c27045e19b139969ef7949a56855a3888 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Delgado <admin@sytue.eu>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(mobile/ios): background remote notifications

A background remote notification (content-available, no alert) wakes the app so it can
fetch what changed from its own servers. The mobile driver now implements the optional
mobile.RemoteNotificationDriver:

- RemoteNotificationsAvailable: the app lists "remote-notification" in
  UIBackgroundModes. Readable from main, before UIKit launches.
- RegisterForRemoteNotifications: asks UIKit for the device token, with no permission
  prompt, and hands it to every caller waiting for it in lowercase hexadecimal (or the
  error UIKit gave). Concurrent callers share one request.
- OnRemoteNotification: the handler of application:didReceiveRemoteNotification:
  fetchCompletionHandler:. The payload is never read. The handler gets a context that is
  cancelled after 25 seconds, and the completion handler is called exactly once: with
  new data, no data or failed as the handler returned, failed when its context was
  cancelled, or failed after a 500 ms grace if the handler does not return, as iOS kills
  an app that never calls it. Protected data availability is asked for on the main
  thread before the handler runs. With no handler the notification fails at once.

Apps without the background mode behave as before. The portable state machine is
tested on every platform; the Objective-C bridge is pinned by source contracts, as it
cannot be compiled outside Xcode.

The delegate has application:didReceiveRemoteNotification:fetchCompletionHandler: only in
an app that declares the mode: runApp adds it, from goApplication:didReceiveRemoteNotification:
fetchCompletionHandler:, before UIApplicationMain. Elsewhere UIKit would warn that the mode
is missing and wake the app for nothing. Without ARC, the copy of the completion handler
is its one reference, released once the handler is called.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JNuJHCzQJGHE9egbBprScr
